\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hark what a sound, 
\par and too divine for hearing,
\par Stirs on the earth and trembles in the air !
\par Is it the thunder of the Lord's appearing?
\par Is it the music of His people's prayer ?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Surely He cometh, and a thousand voices
\par Shout to the saints, and to the deaf are dumb ;
\par Surely He cometh, and the earth rejoices,
\par Glad in His coming who hath sworn : I come !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. This hath He done, and shall we not adore Him?
\par This shall He do, and can we still despair ?
\par Come, let us quickly fling ourselves before Him,
\par Cast at His feet the burden of our care.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Yea, through life, death, through 
\par sorrow and through sinning
\par He shall suffice me, for He hath sufficed :
\par Christ is the end, for Christ was the beginning,
\par Christ the beginning, for the end is Christ.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

